{
  "name": "PAD Robin Data Type Reference (Power Fx)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "date": "2026-10-13",
  "description": "Power Fx edition of the Type Reference 3.1.1: how to write each parameter type in a Power Fx-enabled desktop flow. Text values are $fx'...'; everything else is written as in classic flows unless noted.",
  "rules": [
    "Text values use $fx'value'. Inside, \\' is an apostrophe and \\\\ one backslash; a bare or doubled apostrophe rejects the whole paste.",
    "Expressions start with = inside $fx: $fx'=5', $fx'=Price * Qty', $fx'=\"a\" & \"b\"'.",
    "Interpolation: $fx'Saved ${Count} files'. A literal ${ is $${. No %% escaping: $fx'100% done'.",
    "Booleans may be bare True / False or $fx'=true'; numbers may be bare or $fx'=1'.",
    "Handle/instance variables use bare variable names from previous action outputs. Names are case-sensitive.",
    "Enum values use Module.EnumType.Value, unchanged from classic flows.",
    "Lists are 1-based: $fx'=Index(L, 1)'; count with $fx'=CountRows(L)'. L[0] and L.Count paste but fail at run time.",
    "Empty backticks `` mean the param needs a value filled in."
  ],
  "total_types": 44,
  "types": [
    {
      "type": "String",
      "category": "value",
      "example": "$fx'example'",
      "description": "Text value written $fx'...'",
      "format": "$fx'your_value_here'"
    },
    {
      "type": "Int32",
      "category": "value",
      "example": "1",
      "description": "Integer number, bare value",
      "format": "number or $fx'=expression'"
    },
    {
      "type": "Decimal",
